<table border="0" cellpadding="5" width="550" cellspacing="5" height="400" >
<tr valign="top" height="400" >
<td tEditID="c1r1" style=" background-color:#FFFFFF; bEditID:r3st1; color:#000000; bLabel:main; font-size:12pt; font-family:arial;" aEditID="c1r1" locked="0" >
<![CDATA[<div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;">Dear {!Contact.FirstName},</div><div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial"><br></font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial">Thank you for your interest in undergraduate studies at the Herberger Institute for Design and the Arts School of Music at ASU. As one of the largest universities in the country, the ASU School of Music awards over $2 million to students annually, providing an excellent education at an unbeatable value. ASU's diverse and innovative community is a perfect complement to the personal attention you will receive in the School of Music. With a population of around 750 students, we offer small class sizes, state-of-the-art facilities and one-on-one instruction from world-renowned faculty. &nbsp;We invite you to consider the ASU School of Music for this important step in your music studies.</font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial"><br></font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial">Applications for 2017 admission will be available on the <a href="https://music.asu.edu/admissions/undergraduate-steps-to-apply">School of Music website</a> at the end of August. If you are interested in future study at ASU, please review the information below for what to expect when you are ready to apply. For an idea of the course requirements for the various degree programs offered, select one of the major maps listed <a href="https://webapp4.asu.edu/programs/t5/programs/Keyword/music/undergrad/false">here</a>.</font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial"><br></font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial"><a href="http://students.asu.edu/costs">Tuition and fees</a> at Arizona State University are reasonable, even for non-resident students. Financial aid including academic scholarships is available for both Freshman and Transfer applicants. Freshman applicants can use the Freshman Merit Scholarship Estimator to determine the amount they may be eligible to receive. Transfer applicants may learn about the New American University Transfer Scholarship <a href="http://students.asu.edu/node/7646">here</a>. In addition, music scholarship assistance is also available and awarded based on audition.</font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial"><br></font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial"><b>Reminders for</b> <a href="http://global.asu.edu/future/undergrad"><b>prospective international undergraduate students</b></a>:</font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><ol><li><span style="font-size: 12pt;">If you are from a country whose native language is not English, you must provide proof of English proficiency. Acceptable proof is as follows:&nbsp;</span></li></ol></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><ul><li><span style="font-size: 12pt;">TOEFL score of at least 500 (PBT) or 61 (iBT)</span></li><li><span style="font-size: 12pt;">IELTS overall band score of at least 6.0 with no band below 5.5</span></li><li><span style="font-size: 12pt;">Pearson Test of English (PTE) score of at least 53&nbsp;<br></span></li></ul><div>Because your application is considered incomplete without a passing score in one of the English proficiency exams listed above, it is strongly recommended for prospective applicants to complete and pass their English proficiency exam prior to beginning the application process. Exam scores are accepted for exams taken up to two years prior to the day you submit your application. <b>Applications submitted without a passing TOEFL, IELTS, or PTE score will not be considered for admission</b>. Please visit <a href="http://global.asu.edu/">ASU Global Education</a> for information on the international student application process.</div></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><br></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><span class="Apple-tab-span" style="white-space:pre">	</span>2.&nbsp;</span><span style="font-size: 12pt;">In addition to University tuition and fees, international students <span class="Apple-tab-span" style="white-space:pre">	</span>are required to enroll in the&nbsp;<a href="http://students.asu.edu/healthcoverageoptions">ASU student health&nbsp;insurance&nbsp;plan</a>.&nbsp;More <span class="Apple-tab-span" style="white-space:pre">	</span>information about this requirement can be found here.</span></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial"><br></font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><b>Application Process</b></span></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial"><br></font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><span class="Apple-tab-span" style="white-space:pre">	</span><b>Step 1</b>: Apply to ASU&nbsp;</span></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial"><span class="Apple-tab-span" style="white-space:pre">	</span><b>Step 2</b>: Submit the School of Music Application</font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><ul><li><span style="font-size: 12pt;">You do not need to be admitted to the university prior to submitting your music application (Step 2)</span></li><li><span style="font-size: 12pt;">The School of Music is a separate application from the university. Please visit the <a href="https://music.asu.edu/admissions/undergraduate-steps-to-apply">School of Music Website</a> for more details.</span></li></ul></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial"><span class="Apple-tab-span" style="white-space:pre">	</span><b>Step 3</b>: Audition and Interview</font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><ul><li><span style="font-size: 12pt;">All applicants must perform an audition to be considered for admission to the School of Music.</span></li><li><span style="font-size: 12pt;">On-Campus auditions will not be scheduled until all both application are submitted</span></li><li><span style="font-size: 12pt;">Recorded auditions are acceptable when uploaded <a href="https://music.asu.edu/admissions/undergraduate-recordings-portfolios">online</a>. However, music scholarship consideration is prioritized to those who audition live.</span></li></ul></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial"><br></font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial">Due to the high volume of applicants we receive each year, we recommend that you plan to apply as early as possible.</font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial"><br></font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><b><a href="https://music.asu.edu/admissions/graduate-deadlines-fees">Application Deadline</a></b></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial"><br></font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial"><b>Spring Admission: October 15 for all applicants except those applying to Music Composition.</b></font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial">BM Composition applicants: Application and prescreening portfolio must be received by October 1. Visit <a href="https://music.asu.edu/admissions/undergraduate-recordings-portfolios">our site</a> for more information.</font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial"><br></font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><b>Fall Admission: January 6 for all applicants except those applying to Music Composition.</b></span></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial">BM Composition: Prescreening portfolio must be received by December 1. Visit <a href="https://music.asu.edu/admissions/undergraduate-recordings-portfolios">our site</a> for more information.</font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><br></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial"><b>Audition Dates and Information</b></font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial">For complete audition dates and audition information please visit the <a href="https://music.asu.edu/admissions/undergraduate-auditions">Audition website</a>.</font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial"><br></font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial">Recorded auditions (in lieu of live auditions) must be uploaded <a href="https://music.asu.edu/admissions/undergraduate-recordings-portfolios">online</a> by November 1 for Spring admissions and February 1 for Fall admission. CD/DVD audition recordings are not accepted. To be considered for a music scholarship or teaching assistantship, a live, on-campus audition is preferred.</font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial"><br></font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial">Ad hoc auditions may be scheduled with faculty (required for organ applicants, not available to voice applicants), but must be completed by <b>November 30</b>&nbsp;for spring admission and <b>February 28</b>&nbsp;for fall admission.</font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial"><br></font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial">We welcome you to contact us via email to <a href="mailto:musicadmissions@asu.edu">MusicAdmissions@asu.edu</a> if you have any additional questions. We also encourage you to refer to the School of Music Web site, <a href="https://music.asu.edu">music.asu.edu</a>, as a resource for your admissions questions.</font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial"><br></font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial">Best wishes,</font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial"><br></font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial"><br></font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial">Office of Admissions</font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial">School of Music</font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial"><br></font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial">Herberger Institute for Design and the Arts</font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial">Arizona State University</font></div><div><font face="arial" color="#ffffff">{!Case.Thread_Id}</font></div></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><br></div>]]></td>
</tr>
</table>